# Line-ending policy (2026-09-08 hygiene pass)
#
# Every blob in HEAD is LF-only: no tracked file in the committed tree contains
# a CR.  `core.autocrlf` and `core.eol` are unset, so git itself never converted
# anything; the churn came from Windows-side writing tools (PowerShell
# `Set-Content`/`Out-File`, patch utilities) that rewrote whole files with CRLF.
# Before this pass, 342 of 414 modified tracked files differed from HEAD by line
# endings alone.  Pinning normalization here keeps future adds and checkouts LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The parity ledger tree is hash-bound.  Validators recompute SHA-256 over these
# exact bytes, and two of them currently contain CRLF
# (docs/editor-parity/manifest.json is bound as
# a5182ddaeb88368b293ee55931e6dd7deec989eb62cda57d5c9c09c65b38b053 by the frozen
# legacy state, and docs/editor-parity/schemas/progress-ledger.schema.json also
# carries CRLF).  Converting them on add or checkout would invalidate the frozen
# bindings, so this subtree is stored byte-for-byte.
docs/editor-parity/** -text
docs/gltf-scene-editor-parity-task.md -text
docs/gltf-scene-editor-parity-progress.md -text
docs/gltf-scene-editor-parity-local-progress.md -text

